{"id":"UP-DEBT-pin.allowBuilds.lefthook","type":"DEBT","path":"pnpm-workspace.yaml","title":"allowBuilds: lefthook: true","attrs":{"dep":"lefthook","kind":"pin","section":"allowBuilds","statedReason":""}}
{"id":"UP-DEBT-pin.allowBuilds.msgpackr-extract","type":"DEBT","path":"pnpm-workspace.yaml","title":"allowBuilds: msgpackr-extract: false","attrs":{"dep":"msgpackr-extract","kind":"pin","section":"allowBuilds","statedReason":"Cross-platform boundary for the persistent PTY backend, including ConPTY on Windows. Pulled in by @earendil-works/pi-ai (optional LLM API backend). pnpm lists them only because they ship lifecycle scripts, but those are no-ops we don't need, so we deny them — install still succeeds. JSONL durability calls MoveFileExW with write-through publication on Windows. Consumers pin 3.1.1: Koffi 3.3.2's source build fails under GCC 13 when optional prebuilts are omitted. Upgrade all consumers together after the replacement passes that build and the release packed-install check. The Python runtime deploy includes the reviewed workspace postinstall that restores the executable bit on node-pty's macOS spawn helper. electron-builder pulls in the optional Squirrel.Windows helper, whose install script only selects its bundled 7-Zip executable. Desktop ships Windows through NSIS, so that mutation is not part of our build. Store-index rewriting only needs msgpackr's portable JavaScript codec."}}
{"id":"UP-DEBT-pin.minimumReleaseAgeExclude.pnpm@11.28.5","type":"DEBT","path":"pnpm-workspace.yaml","title":"minimumReleaseAgeExclude: pnpm@11.28.5","attrs":{"dep":"pnpm","kind":"pin","section":"minimumReleaseAgeExclude","statedReason":"Native Codex and Claude tests qualify this exact release with its local patches. Office engines and their API are qualified and released together by the kit repository. Fresh pi-ai releases carry the model catalog updates that are the whole point of bumping it; waiting out the release age would defeat that. This addon release recognizes the Electron 44.7.0 Node/V8 fingerprint used by Desktop. The active pnpm supply-chain policy blocks this reviewed runtime closure until its release-age window expires unless every exact package is exempt. All platform aliases resolve to the @openai/codex package name, so their reviewed exact versions must share one version-union policy entry. The native computer-use provider pins this reviewed upstream runtime closure. The package manager is a workspace devDependency, so its own exact pin must be exempt from the release-age window that guards other packages."}}
{"id":"UP-DEBT-pin.overrides.extract-zip_yauzl","type":"DEBT","path":"pnpm-workspace.yaml","title":"overrides: 'extract-zip>yauzl': '3.4.0'","attrs":{"dep":"yauzl","kind":"pin","section":"overrides","statedReason":""}}
